      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the movement is more nuanced—like shrink wrap loosening or small items migrating across a pallet—then we move beyond simple kinetic vibration into the realm of environmental stresses and material physics. Temperature fluctuations and humidity changes can cause materials to expand or contract at different rates, leading to stresses within the packaging itself. Furthermore, even minor air currents, perhaps from HVAC systems or door drafts, can exert enough force on lightweight items to cause them to shift or dislodge. These subtle environmental pressures can mimic the appearance of deliberate tampering.",
      "source": "target",
